], "overall": "A faithful, literal rendering that rightly keeps the hard Septuagintal readings (v.8 'o irmão não resgata, o homem resgatará', v.9's dangling 'E o preço', v.14 'na sua boca', v.15b) without smoothing them toward the Hebrew. The faults are all minor: a flattened correlative in v.3, a noun turned into a clause in v.5, a temporal 'desde' for a separative 'a' in v.15b, 'nada' for 'non ... ómnia' in v.18, and a dropped 'ipsíus' in v.19. In v.19 'te' reads tibi as the 'tu' of v.17, which is coherent given the vós convention for God. Pointing marks match the Latin throughout (a single * in every verse, no † or ‡)."}
